No developer fee.

The Equihash solver (Wagner's algorithm, CUDA) and its host code are original work.
Correctness references used for the tests only (not linked into the miner):
  - Kerrigan Core (MIT, github.com/kerrigan-network/kerrigan): src/crypto/equihash.cpp,
    whose solver produced the reference solutions in src/eq_vectors.h;
  - libsodium / Python hashlib: BLAKE2b known answers.
The stratum client (json.h, tls_conn.*) comes from FiloMiner (same author, Apache-2.0).

The Windows release zip also contains third-party components (not in this repository):
  - OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), statically linked into krgnminer.exe (MSYS2 MINGW64 package);
  - the MinGW-w64 runtime, winpthreads and libstdc++/libgcc (permissive licences, GCC
    Runtime Library Exception), statically linked into krgnminer.exe;
  - cudart64_12.dll, the NVIDIA CUDA runtime, redistributed under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
    EULA (used by kgpu.dll);
  - ca-bundle.crt, the Mozilla CA certificate bundle (MPL-2.0), from MSYS2.
